Fix: two debug asserts in MapPoint.remove_frame_view that cannot hold for its callers

remove_frame_view() performs its removal in two stages: it validates and drops the
back-reference while holding _lock_features, then calls frame.remove_point_match(idx)
afterwards, outside the lock. Both __debug__ asserts inside the locked section state
conditions that depend on that later call, or on what the caller did beforehand -- and
the two callers disagree, so no single pre-state satisfies both.

1) assert self == frame.get_point_match(idx)
   Frame.clean_outlier_map_points() (frame.py:1029) sets self.points[i] = None BEFORE
   calling, so the match is already gone and the assert fires. On KITTI 06 this aborts
   the run at frame 13, the first frame where pose optimization reports outliers
   ("found 5 bad points").
   -> relaxed to accept the already-cleared case, while still catching a genuine
      mismatch (a *different* point at that index fails both comparisons).

2) assert not self in frame.get_points()
   Frame.remove_frame_views() (frame.py:918) does NOT pre-null the entry, so the point
   is legitimately still present and the assert fires. It is a post-condition being
   checked before the removal it describes; it only passed for caller (1) by accident,
   because that caller happened to pre-null.
   -> rewritten as the invariant the comment actually describes ("no multiple
      instances"): the point occupies at most one index. Holds for both callers,
      and still fails if the same point is genuinely matched at two indices.
   Cost is unchanged: the original "in" test was already an O(n) __eq__ scan.

Both relaxed rather than deleted, and PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1 was rejected, because that
would disable every __debug__ assert in pySLAM -- and these asserts have been useful.

The work after the asserts is correct for both callers: Frame.remove_point_match() is
an idempotent "self.points[idx] = None" (frame.py:895).

Upstream: luigifreda/pyslam master @ a5ff256 (no release tags exist).

diff --git a/pyslam/slam/map_point.py b/pyslam/slam/map_point.py
index 05164f9..670369c 100644
--- a/pyslam/slam/map_point.py
+++ b/pyslam/slam/map_point.py
@@ -278,11 +278,11 @@ class MapPointBase(object):
             # remove point from frame
             if idx is not None:
                 if __debug__:
-                    assert self == frame.get_point_match(idx)
+                    assert frame.get_point_match(idx) in (self, None)
                 frame_remove_point_match = True
                 if __debug__:
                     assert (
-                        not self in frame.get_points()
+                        sum(1 for q in frame.get_points() if q == self) <= 1
                     )  # checking there are no multiple instances
             else:
                 frame_remove_point = True
